2026-09-27T04:47:52.4338894Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4339098Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4339402Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4339685Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4339779Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4339999Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4340114Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4340261Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4340640Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4340862Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4340969Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4341236Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4341404Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4341548Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4341946Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4342292Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4342942Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4343474Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4343587Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4344002Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4344518Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4344797Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4345085Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4345470Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4345557Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4345740Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4345845Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4347123Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4348644Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4348880Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4349344Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4349793Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4350366Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4350933Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4351364Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4351625Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4352063Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4352316Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4423411Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4424648Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4426298Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4426956Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4427856Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:52.4428072Z 
